11	// AppKit app (a command-line tool has no `NSApp.terminate` to route into) AND it
12	// must install a capture tap (no tap, no IOProc to abandon, nothing at stake).
13	// Everything is read with comments stripped — prose describing the trap is not
14	// an implementation of it, nor evidence against one.
15	//
16	// Three arms:
17	//   1. nothing anywhere routes those signals — any of the three mechanisms a Mac
18	//      app plausibly uses counts as routing (`DispatchSource.makeSignalSource`,
19	//      `sigaction`, a direct `signal(SIGTERM, …)` handler);
20	//   2. routing exists but one of the three signals is named nowhere in the
21	//      sources — the unrouted one stays fatal by default;
22	//   3. `SIG_IGN` comes after the source is resumed — until the default action is
23	//      ignored, a signal landing in the gap still terminates the process outright.
24	//
